              <g><line x1={P.l} x2={P.w - P.r} y1={py(v, panelMax.share)} y2={py(v, panelMax.share)} class="ph__grid" /><text x={P.l - 6} y={py(v, panelMax.share) + 3} text-anchor="end" class="ph__svg-label">{v}%</text></g>
            ))}
            <path d={linePath((f) => f.share, panelMax.share)} class="ph__line" />
            {fleet.map((f) => <circle cx={px(f.year)} cy={py(f.share, panelMax.share)} r="2" class="ph__pt"><title>{f.year}: {f.share.toFixed(1)}% plug-in</title></circle>)}
            <text x={px(2025) + 4} y={py(fleetNow.share, panelMax.share) - 8} class="ph__svg-val">{fleetNow.share.toFixed(1)}%</text>
            <text x={px(2040)} y={py(fleetEnd.share, panelMax.share) - 8} text-anchor="end" class="ph__svg-val">{fleetEnd.share.toFixed(1)}%</text>
            {[2025, 2030, 2035, 2040].map((y) => <text x={px(y)} y={P.h - 8} text-anchor="middle" class="ph__svg-label">{y}</text>)}
          </svg>
          <p>From fewer than 3 in 100 to almost 4 in 10.</p>
        </div>
        <figcaption>US cars and light trucks in use (personal and fleet). 2025 is EIA’s modelled base year; 2026–2040 is EIA’s Annual Energy Outlook 2026 Counterfactual Baseline, a policy-dependent scenario, not a forecast. Heavy trucks and buses are not included.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <p class="ph__next">So where do these {mil(fleetNow.ev)} plug-in vehicles charge today? <a href="#usa" data-jump-slide="1" class="ph__state-jump">02 · Charging today</a></p>

