                <span data-st-stations={s.code}>{fmt(s.groups.public.all.stations)} stations · public access · {s.usPortShare.toFixed(1)}% of US public ports</span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <aside class="ph__summary">
              <div class="ph__metric">
                <span>Public charging ports · {s.name} (#{s.meta.slideIdx} in USA)</span>
                <strong>{fmt(s.pubPorts)}</strong>
                <small>{fmt(s.groups.public.all.stations)} stations · {fmt(s.groups.public.all.dc)} DC fast ({s.dcShare.toFixed(1)}%) · {fmt(s.groups.public.all.l2)} Level 2</small>
              </div>
              <div class="ph__metric">
                <span>Registered plug-in fleet · 2025</span>
                <strong>{fmt(s.plugins)}</strong>
                <small>{fmt(s.now.bev)} battery EVs ({pct(s.now.bev, s.now.total)} of fleet) + {fmt(s.now.phev)} plug-in hybrids · <b>{s.evsPerPort.toFixed(1)} EVs / public port</b></small>
              </div>

              <!-- State Port Anatomy Visualizer -->
              <div class="ph__viz-box">
                <div class="ph__viz-head">
                  <b>{s.name} port anatomy ({fmt(s.allPorts)} total ports)</b>
                  <span>Breakdown by access, charger speed &amp; Tesla share</span>
                </div>
                <div class="ph__stack-row">
                  <div class="ph__stack-meta"><span>1. Access</span><span><b>{pct(s.pubPorts, s.allPorts)}</b> public / <b>{pct(s.privPorts, s.allPorts)}</b> private ({fmt(s.privPorts)})</span></div>
                  <div class="ph__stack-bar">
                    <i class="is-other" style={`width:${(s.pubPorts / s.allPorts) * 100}%`}></i>
                    <i class="is-phev" style={`width:${(s.privPorts / s.allPorts) * 100}%`}></i>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ph__stack-row">
                  <div class="ph__stack-meta"><span>2. Public speed split</span><span><b>{s.dcShare.toFixed(1)}%</b> DC fast ({fmt(s.groups.public.all.dc)}) / <b>{s.l2Share.toFixed(1)}%</b> L2 ({fmt(s.groups.public.all.l2)})</span></div>
                  <div class="ph__stack-bar">
                    <i class="is-tesla" style={`width:${s.dcShare}%`}></i>
                    <i class="is-other" style={`width:${s.l2Share}%`}></i>
                  </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ph__stack-row">
                  <div class="ph__stack-meta"><span>3. Public DC fast control</span><span><b>{s.teslaDcShare.toFixed(1)}%</b> Tesla ({fmt(s.groups.public.tesla.dc)} of {fmt(s.groups.public.all.dc)})</span></div>
                  <div class="ph__stack-bar">
                    <i class="is-tesla" style={`width:${s.teslaDcShare}%`}></i>
                    <i class="is-other" style={`width:${100 - s.teslaDcShare}%`}></i>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>

              <div class="ph__energy">
                <span>Modeled EV electricity · {s.name} · 2024</span>
                <strong>{fmt(s.energy.total)} GWh</strong>
                <div class="ph__stack-bar" style="margin: 4px 0;">
                  <i class="is-tesla" style={`width:${(s.energy.bev / s.energy.total) * 100}%`}></i>
                  <i class="is-phev" style={`width:${(s.energy.phev / s.energy.total) * 100}%`}></i>
                </div>
                <p>EIA SEDS Table F56 estimate across home, workplace &amp; public charging: <b>{fmt(s.energy.bev)} GWh</b> BEV + <b>{fmt(s.energy.phev)} GWh</b> PHEV.</p>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>

          <!-- State Networks + State Vehicle Growth Visualizers -->
          <div class="ph__viz-grid">
            <div class="ph__viz-card">
              <div class="ph__viz-head">
                <h2>Leading charging networks in {s.name}</h2>
                <span>Public ports by AFDC network category in {s.name} (out of {fmt(s.pubPorts)} public ports)</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ph__net-chart">
                {s.stateNets.map((n) => (
                  <div class="ph__net-row">
                    <div class="ph__net-label">
                      <b>{n.name}</b>
                      <span>{fmt(n.ports)} ports ({n.share.toFixed(1)}% of {s.code})</span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ph__net-bar-track">
                      <i
                        class={n.name.includes('Tesla') ? 'is-tesla' : 'is-other'}
                        style={`width:${(n.ports / s.maxStateNet) * 100}%`}
                      />
                    </div>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
              <p class="ph__note">
                <b>{s.meta.contextTitle}:</b> {s.meta.contextBody} Reference: <a href={s.meta.planUrl}>{s.meta.planLabel}</a>.
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="ph__viz-card">
              <div class="ph__viz-head">
                <h2>How fast {s.name} is switching (2016–2025)</h2>
                <span>{s.cagr.toFixed(1)}% annual BEV CAGR · {s.mult2025.toFixed(1)}× expansion since 2016 · +{fmt(s.yoyGain)} BEVs in 2024–25 (+{s.yoyPct.toFixed(1)}%)</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ph__history" style="margin-bottom: 16px;">
                {sYears.map((yr) => (
                  <div>
                    <span>{yr.y}</span>
                    <div class="ph__track">
                      <i style={`width:${(yr.bev / s.now.bev) * 100}%`} title={`${yr.y} BEV: ${fmt(yr.bev)}`}></i>
                    </div>
                    <b>{fmt(yr.bev)} BEV</b>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>

              <div class="ph__shift-row" style="margin-top: 8px;">
                <div class="ph__stack-meta">
                  <span><b>2025 Light-duty ({million(s.now.total)})</b></span>
                  <span><b>{pct(s.now.bev, s.now.total)}</b> BEV ({kfmt(s.now.bev)}) · <b>{pct(s.now.phev, s.now.total)}</b> PHEV ({kfmt(s.now.phev)})</span>
                </div>
                <div class="ph__stack-bar">
                  <i class="is-tesla" style={`width:${(s.now.bev / s.now.total) * 100}%`}></i>
                  <i class="is-phev" style={`width:${(s.now.phev / s.now.total) * 100}%`}></i>
                  <i class="is-fuel" style={`width:${(s.now.fuel / s.now.total) * 100}%`}></i>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p class="ph__legend" style="margin-top:10px;">
                <span class="ph__key ph__key--tesla">Battery EV</span>
                <span class="ph__key ph__key--phev">Plug-in hybrid</span>
                <span class="ph__key ph__key--fuel">Fuel-powered</span>
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          {s.code === 'NY' && (
            <div class="ph__viz-card" style="margin-top: 24px;" id="ny-detail">
              <div class="ph__viz-head">
                <h2>Inside New York City: where the street-parked half can charge</h2>
                <span>NYC holds {pct(data.city.groups.public.all.ports, s.pubPorts)} of New York State’s public ports ({fmt(data.city.groups.public.all.ports)} of {fmt(s.pubPorts)})</span>
              </div>
              <div class="ph__ny-grid">
                <div>
                  <div class="ph__filters">
                    <label>
                      Borough
                      <select id="ph-borough">
                        <option value="all">All five boroughs</option>
                        {data.city.boroughs.map((b) => (
                          <option value={b.name}>{b.name} ({fmt(b.groups.public.all.ports)} ports)</option>
                        ))}
                      </select>
                    </label>
                    <label>
                      Charger type
                      <select id="ph-city-type">
                        <option value="all">All public stations</option>
                        <option value="dc">Has DC fast</option>
                        <option value="ac">AC only</option>
                      </select>
                    </label>
                  </div>
                  <div class="ph__mapbox ph__mapbox--city" data-map="NYC" role="region" aria-label="Zoomable map of New York City public charging stations"></div>
                  <p class="ph__legend">
                    <span class="ph__key ph__key--tesla">Tesla networks</span>
                    <span class="ph__key ph__key--other">Other networks</span>
                    <span>Choose a borough to zoom to it · charger type filters the dots</span>
                  </p>
                  <p id="ph-city-result" class="ph__selection" aria-live="polite">
                    NYC · {fmt(data.city.groups.public.all.stations)} public stations · {fmt(data.city.groups.public.all.ports)} ports ({fmt(data.city.groups.public.all.dc)} DC fast)
                  </p>
                </div>

                <div class="ph__ny-copy">
                  <div class="ph__viz-box">
                    <div class="ph__viz-head">
                      <b>5-Borough public port distribution (AC vs. DC fast)</b>
                      <span>Select a borough on the left to isolate stations on the map</span>
                    </div>
                    {data.city.boroughs.map((b) => {
                      const ac = b.groups.public.all.l1 + b.groups.public.all.l2;
                      const dc = b.groups.public.all.dc;
                      const tot = b.groups.public.all.ports;
                      return (
                        <div class="ph__boro-row" data-borough-row={b.name}>
                          <div class="ph__boro-meta">
                            <b>{b.name}</b>
                            <span>{fmt(tot)} ports · {fmt(b.groups.public.all.stations)} stations ({fmt(dc)} DC fast / {fmt(ac)} AC)</span>
                          </div>
                          <div class="ph__net-bar-track">
                            <i class="is-tesla" style={`width:${(dc / maxBoroPorts) * 100}%`} title={`${b.name} DC fast: ${fmt(dc)}`}></i>
                            <i class="is-other" style={`width:${(ac / maxBoroPorts) * 100}%`} title={`${b.name} AC: ${fmt(ac)}`}></i>
                          </div>
                        </div>
                      );
                    })}
                  </div>

                  <div class="ph__gauge-grid">
                    <div class="ph__energy">
                      <span>Observed use · NYC curbside pilot</span>
                      <strong>70%</strong>
                      <div class="ph__stack-bar" style="margin:4px 0;"><i class="is-tesla" style="width:70%"></i></div>
                      <p>Average plugged-in occupancy reported by NYC DOT (Aug 2024) across 100 curbside chargers at 35 sites.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ph__energy">
                      <span>NYC car-owner parking reliance</span>
                      <strong>50%</strong>
                      <div class="ph__stack-bar" style="margin:4px 0;"><i class="is-phev" style="width:50%"></i></div>
                      <p>Half of NYC car-owning households rely on on-street parking (NYC DOT, Aug 2026), requiring shared neighborhood charging.</p>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  <div class="ph__table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Public charging by borough">
                    <table>
                      <caption>Public charging by borough</caption>
                      <thead><tr><th>Borough</th><th>Stations</th><th>AC ports</th><th>DC fast</th><th>All ports</th></tr></thead>
                      <tbody>
                        {data.city.boroughs.map((b) => (
                          <tr data-borough-row={b.name}>
                            <th scope="row">{b.name}</th>
                            <td>{fmt(b.groups.public.all.stations)}</td>
                            <td>{fmt(b.groups.public.all.l1 + b.groups.public.all.l2)}</td>
                            <td>{fmt(b.groups.public.all.dc)}</td>
                            <td>{fmt(b.groups.public.all.ports)}</td>
                          </tr>
                        ))}
                      </tbody>
                    </table>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          )}

          <footer class="ph__sources">
            Sources: <a href={sources.afdc}>DOE AFDC inventory</a> (snapshot 18 Oct 2026); <a href={sources.regs + '?year=2025'}>AFDC 2016–2025 vehicle registrations</a>; <a href={sources.stateEnergy}>EIA SEDS Table F56 (2024)</a>; <a href={s.meta.planUrl}>{s.meta.planLabel}</a>.
          </footer>
        </section>
      );
    })}

    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <!-- SLIDE 05: COMPARISON OF THE THREE STATES                           -->
    <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
    <section id="comparison" class="ph__slide" data-slide="5" aria-labelledby="comparison-title" hidden>
      <div class="ph__heading">
        <p class="ph__kicker">06 · The three states side by side</p>
        <h1 id="comparison-title" tabindex="-1">Three states, three tests</h1>
        <p>California has the most of everything, New York the fewest cars per plug but a city that cannot charge at home, Florida the fastest growth and the most cars per plug. Read across each row to see which state each claim in the text rests on.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- 3-State Side-by-Side Maps -->
      <div class="ph__state-grid">
        {states.map((s, i) => (
          <div class="ph__state-card">
            <div class="ph__state-title">
              <span>0{i + 1}</span>
              <h2><a href={`#${s.meta.slug}`} data-jump-slide={s.meta.slideIdx} class="ph__state-jump">{s.name}</a></h2>
            </div>
            <p class="ph__state-role">{roleOf[s.code].claim}</p>
            <div class="ph__state-number">
              {fmt(s.pubPorts)}<span>public ports ({fmt(s.groups.public.all.stations)} stations)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ph__bar" role="img" aria-label={`${s.name}: ${fmt(s.groups.public.all.dc)} DC fast and ${fmt(s.groups.public.all.l2)} Level 2 ports`}>
              <span class="ph__fill ph__fill--tesla" style={`width:${s.dcShare}%`}></span>
            </div>
            <p class="ph__note">
              <b>{s.dcShare.toFixed(1)}% DC fast</b> ({fmt(s.groups.public.all.dc)}) · <b>{s.evsPerPort.toFixed(1)}</b> plug-in EVs per public port
            </p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>

      <!-- 6-Metric Visual Comparison Dashboard -->
      <div class="ph__viz-card" style="margin-top:24px;">
        <div class="ph__viz-head">
          <h2>1. Six-metric infrastructure &amp; demand comparison (CA vs. NY vs. FL)</h2>
          <span>Proportional bar scales normalized to the leading state in each category</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ph__metric-grid">
          {metricComparisons.map((m) => {
            const maxVal = Math.max(...m.values.map((v) => v.val));
            return (
              <div class="ph__mcard">
                <div class="ph__mcard-title">{m.label}</div>
                {m.values.map((v) => (
                  <div class="ph__mrow">
                    <span class="ph__mcode">{v.code}</span>
                    <div class="ph__mtrack">
                      <i
                        class={v.code === 'CA' ? 'is-tesla' : v.code === 'FL' ? 'is-phev' : 'is-other'}
                        style={`width:${(v.val / maxVal) * 100}%`}
                      />
                    </div>
                    <b class="ph__mval">{v.text}</b>
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            );
          })}
        </div>
        <p class="ph__note">
          ¹ 2025 registered battery EVs + plug-in hybrids divided by October 2026 public ports: a cross-year indicator, not a queue or capacity measure. ² EIA modeled vehicle electricity across all locations, including home charging; 1 GWh = 1 million kWh.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- How fast each state is switching -->
      <div class="ph__viz-grid" style="margin-top:20px;">
        <div class="ph__viz-card">
          <div class="ph__viz-head">
            <h2>2. Absolute BEV fleet growth (2016 → 2025)</h2>
            <span>California’s early scale lead vs. Florida and New York volume</span>
          </div>
          <svg class="ph__svg ph__line-chart" viewBox={`0 0 ${chartW} ${chartH}`} role="img" aria-label="Absolute battery electric vehicle registrations from 2016 to 2025">
            {[0, 0.25, 0.5, 0.75, 1].map((t) => {
              const y = padT + (1 - t) * (chartH - padT - padB);
              const val = t * maxBev;
              return (
                <g>
                  <line x1={padL} y1={y.toFixed(1)} x2={chartW - padR} y2={y.toFixed(1)} stroke="var(--_tokens---color--line)" stroke-dasharray={t === 0 ? undefined : '2,3'} />
                  <text x={padL - 6} y={(y + 3).toFixed(1)} text-anchor="end" class="ph__svg-label">{kfmt(val)}</text>
                </g>
              );
            })}
            {years.map((yr) => (
              <text x={xForYear(yr).toFixed(1)} y={chartH - 6} text-anchor="middle" class="ph__svg-label">{yr}</text>
            ))}
            {trajectories.map((tr) => (
              <g>
                <path d={tr.absPath} fill="none" stroke={tr.color} stroke-width="2.2" stroke-dasharray={tr.dash} />
                {tr.pts.map((p) => (
                  <circle cx={p.x.toFixed(1)} cy={p.yAbs.toFixed(1)} r="3.2" fill={tr.color}>
                    <title>{tr.name} ({p.y}): {fmt(p.bev)} battery EVs</title>
                  </circle>
                ))}
                <text
                  x={(tr.pts[3].x + 6).toFixed(1)}
                  y={(tr.pts[3].yAbs + (tr.code === 'NY' ? 6 : tr.code === 'FL' ? -3 : 3)).toFixed(1)}
                  class="ph__svg-val"
                  fill={tr.color}
                >
                  {tr.code} {kfmt(tr.pts[3].bev)}
                </text>
              </g>
            ))}
          </svg>
        </div>

        <div class="ph__viz-card">
          <div class="ph__viz-head">
            <h2>3. Indexed BEV acceleration (2016 = 1.0× baseline)</h2>
            <span>Relative growth multiplier: FL ({trajectories[2].mult2025.toFixed(1)}×) &amp; NY ({trajectories[1].mult2025.toFixed(1)}×) outpace CA ({trajectories[0].mult2025.toFixed(1)}×)</span>
          </div>
          <svg class="ph__svg ph__line-chart" viewBox={`0 0 ${chartW} ${chartH}`} role="img" aria-label="Indexed battery electric vehicle growth multiplier from 2016 baseline to 2025">
            {[1, 5, 10, 14].map((m) => {
              const y = yForMult(m);
              return (
                <g>
                  <line x1={padL} y1={y.toFixed(1)} x2={chartW - padR} y2={y.toFixed(1)} stroke="var(--_tokens---color--line)" stroke-dasharray={m === 1 ? undefined : '2,3'} />
                  <text x={padL - 6} y={(y + 3).toFixed(1)} text-anchor="end" class="ph__svg-label">{m}×</text>
                </g>
              );
            })}
            {years.map((yr) => (
              <text x={xForYear(yr).toFixed(1)} y={chartH - 6} text-anchor="middle" class="ph__svg-label">{yr}</text>
            ))}
            {trajectories.map((tr) => (
              <g>
                <path d={tr.idxPath} fill="none" stroke={tr.color} stroke-width="2.2" stroke-dasharray={tr.dash} />
                {tr.pts.map((p) => (
                  <circle cx={p.x.toFixed(1)} cy={p.yIdx.toFixed(1)} r="3.2" fill={tr.color}>
                    <title>{tr.name} ({p.y}): {p.mult.toFixed(1)}× 2016 baseline ({fmt(p.bev)} BEVs)</title>
                  </circle>
                ))}
                <text
                  x={(tr.pts[3].x + 6).toFixed(1)}
                  y={(tr.pts[3].yIdx + (tr.code === 'NY' ? 8 : tr.code === 'FL' ? -3 : 3)).toFixed(1)}
                  class="ph__svg-val"
                  fill={tr.color}
                >
                  {tr.code} {tr.mult2025.toFixed(1)}×
                </text>
              </g>
            ))}
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Full 9-Measure Infrastructure & Electricity Comparison Table -->
      <div class="ph__table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Infrastructure, vehicles and electricity table">
        <table>
          <caption>Infrastructure, vehicles and electricity · three-state summary</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Measure</th>{states.map((s) => <th scope="col">{s.name}</th>)}</tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Public stations / private stations</th>{states.map((s) => <td>{fmt(s.groups.public.all.stations)} / {fmt(s.groups.private.all.stations)}</td>)}</tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Public ports: Level 1 / Level 2 / DC fast</th>{states.map((s) => <td>{fmt(s.groups.public.all.l1)} / {fmt(s.groups.public.all.l2)} / {fmt(s.groups.public.all.dc)}</td>)}</tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Reported private ports</th>{states.map((s) => <td>{fmt(s.groups.private.all.ports)}</td>)}</tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Tesla public ports / other public ports</th>{states.map((s) => <td>{fmt(s.groups.public.tesla.ports)} / {fmt(s.groups.public.other.ports)}</td>)}</tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Battery EVs / plug-in hybrids · 2025</th>{states.map((s) => <td>{fmt(s.now.bev)} / {fmt(s.now.phev)}</td>)}</tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Plug-in vehicles per public port¹</th>{states.map((s) => <td>{s.evsPerPort.toFixed(1)}</td>)}</tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">BEV share of light-duty fleet · 2025</th>{states.map((s) => <td>{pct(s.now.bev, s.now.total)}</td>)}</tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">BEV increase · 2024–25</th>{states.map((s) => <td>+{fmt(s.yoyGain)} / +{s.yoyPct.toFixed(1)}%</td>)}</tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">EV electricity · 2024 · GWh²</th>{states.map((s) => <td>{fmt(s.energy.total)}</td>)}</tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <div class="ph__conclusion">
        <h2>What the three states show together</h2>
        <ol>
          <li><b>The shift is real and uneven.</b> Battery-electric cars grew {states.map((s) => `${s.mult2025.toFixed(1)}× in ${s.name}`).join(', ').replace(/, ([^,]*)$/, ' and $1')} since 2016.</li>
          <li><b>Plugs are not keeping pace everywhere.</b> Between {Math.min(...states.map((s) => s.evsPerPort)).toFixed(1)} and {Math.max(...states.map((s) => s.evsPerPort)).toFixed(1)} plug-in vehicles share each public port. The pressure is highest in Florida, which is also growing fastest.</li>
          <li><b>Counting plugs is not enough.</b> New York has the most plugs per car and still cannot serve the half of its city that parks on the street. Where the chargers are, and what surrounds them, matters as much as how many there are. That is the question the next section, The Architecture of the Stop, takes up.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>

      <footer class="ph__sources">Sources: <a href={sources.afdc}>DOE AFDC station inventory</a>, snapshot 18 Oct 2026; <a href={sources.regs + '?year=2016'}>AFDC registrations 2016</a>, <a href={sources.regs + '?year=2020'}>2020</a>, <a href={sources.regs + '?year=2024'}>2024</a>, <a href={sources.regs + '?year=2025'}>2025</a>; <a href={sources.stateEnergy}>EIA SEDS Table F56 (2024)</a>.</footer>
    </section>

